---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Uses" description="The hardware and software I use every day." activeNav="uses">
  <div class="content">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2 class="section-title">Uses</h2>
      <p class="section-desc">The hardware and software I use every day. I update this page when something changes.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="uses-section">
      <h3>Machines</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>MacBook Pro M4 Pro</strong> (14-core, 24GB, 500GB) running macOS 27. My main development machine. Its name is skynet.</li>
        <li><strong>Minisforum UM790 Pro</strong> running Ubuntu 24.04 LTS. My Linux development box and local model server. It runs my self-hosted services and the open-weight models they use, and it never sleeps. Its name is gayaprime.</li>
        <li><strong>iPhone 17 Pro</strong> for iOS testing and LiDAR capture.</li>
        <li><strong>iPad Pro 13&quot;</strong> (M4) for reading, sketching, and the occasional second screen.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="uses-section">
      <h3>Editor and Terminal</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Claude Code</strong> in Ghostty for most of my work. I use the editor mostly to read diffs.</li>
        <li><strong>VS Code</strong> for everything that isn&apos;t Swift.</li>
        <li><strong>Xcode</strong> for iOS and macOS work.</li>
        <li><strong>Ghostty</strong> as the terminal, with zsh, starship, zoxide, and fzf.</li>
        <li><strong>Obsidian</strong> for notes, synced with Obsidian Sync.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="uses-section">
      <h3>Languages</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Rust</strong> for CLI tools that must be fast and small. domain-check and contextsmith are both Rust.</li>
        <li><strong>Swift</strong> for iOS and macOS. SwiftUI first, and UIKit where SwiftUI cannot do the job. Meontor, Doorframe, and Photogram are all Swift 6.</li>
        <li><strong>Go</strong> for backend services, such as Switchboard Gateway.</li>
        <li><strong>TypeScript</strong> for the web. Astro for this site, SvelteKit for the app sites, Next.js for Periodiq.</li>
        <li><strong>Python</strong> for backends and ML. FastAPI for ChannelOS and Loot, and scripts on the Linux box.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="uses-section">
      <h3>Infra</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Docker Compose</strong> for every service that needs a database or a queue. PostgreSQL, Redis, Kafka, and Open WebUI, all in containers on gayaprime.</li>
        <li><strong>Tailscale</strong> to reach the Linux box from my laptop and phone. Nothing on it is exposed to the internet.</li>
        <li><strong>GitHub</strong> for code, releases, CI, and issues.</li>
        <li><strong>Vercel</strong> for the app websites. This site is on GitHub Pages.</li>
        <li><strong>Homebrew</strong> on the Mac, <code>apt</code> + <code>cargo install</code> + Docker on the Linux box. I do not install Python packages globally.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="uses-section">
      <h3>AI</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Claude</strong> every day: Claude Code in the terminal and the desktop app for everything else.</li>
        <li><strong>ChatGPT</strong> and <strong>Perplexity</strong> for a second opinion and for search.</li>
        <li><strong>Ollama</strong> on gayaprime. The default model is <code>gemma4:26b</code>, a 26B mixture-of-experts model that runs on the integrated GPU. I use Qwen2.5-VL for vision. Open WebUI is the chat interface.</li>
        <li><strong>Apple FoundationModels</strong> for on-device generation in my iOS apps.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="uses-section">
      <h3>Hardware around the desk</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>LG 4K monitors</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>NuPhy</strong> mechanical keyboard.</li>
        <li><strong>Logitech MX Master 3</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>AirPods Pro</strong> and <strong>Sony WH-1000XM4</strong>.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="uses-section">
      <h3>At work</h3>
      <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px;">
        Full-stack developer at <a href="https://www.centralsquare.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CentralSquare Technologies</a>, building public administration, public safety, and justice software.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Visual Studio</strong> (17 / 19 / 22) for C# and C++.</li>
        <li><strong>PowerShell 7</strong> + Windows Terminal + WSL Debian.</li>
        <li><strong>GitHub Copilot</strong> with Claude and Codex backends.</li>
        <li>C#, C++, SQL, and some VBScript.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
